      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I don't take a personal stance, but research suggests that a balanced approach that encompasses both perspectives can be the most effective. By exploring both the celebrations of national triumphs and the acknowledgment of systemic injustices, students can gain a more nuanced understanding of history and its complexities. This approach can help foster empathy, critical thinking, and integrity, ultimately preparing students for a better-informed engagement with the world.",
